fb: give the direct-scan path its own counters (0277)

zcPresent() returns from the scanout branch before the zero-copy counters are
reached, so kern.sweet_fb reported zc_frames/zc_us/scan_replaced as zero even
while scanout was running, and the only visible trace was a one-shot ILog on
the first frame. Any measurement of the scanout path therefore had no data.

Add three counters and a submit-time pair:

  scanout_frames    scanoutPresent() accepted the frame (a submit, not a display)
  scanout_declines  it refused (capacity, IOVA, geometry, pipe), frame copied
  scanout_latched   zcPoll() saw the flush bits clear, i.e. reached the panel
  scanout_us        mean time inside scanoutPresent(), max per window

scanout_frames - scanout_latched is the queue depth that is not being retired;
scanout_latched against the panel rate says whether the pipe or the producer is
the limit. Neither number existed before.

